(D1) raw-coh's consec-argmax = Dirichlet/Fejer alignment, NOT measS7
========================================================================
  Among NON-consec shapes, top-5 by each functional:
   by measS7 : [[0, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8], [0, 2, 4, 6, 7, 8, 10, 12], [0, 1, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 9], [0, 1, 2, 4, 5, 6, 7, 10], [0, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9]]
   by raw-coh: [[0, 1, 2, 3, 9, 10, 11, 12], [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 8], [0, 1, 2, 3, 8, 9, 10, 11], [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 10, 11, 12], [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 9, 10, 11]]
   by fejer  : [[0, 1, 3, 4, 6, 7, 11, 12], [0, 1, 5, 7, 8, 10, 11, 12], [0, 1, 2, 4, 5, 7, 11, 12], [0, 1, 4, 6, 7, 9, 10, 12], [0, 1, 5, 6, 8, 9, 11, 12]]
   overlap(measS7-top5, rawcoh-top5)=0/5   overlap(measS7-top5, fejer-top5)=0/5
   global argmax fejer = [0, 1, 3, 4, 6, 7, 11, 12] (consec? False)
   global argmax raw-coh = [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7] (consec? True)
  INTERP: consec is the joint PEAK of measS7 AND of the (trivial) Fejer/
  Dirichlet alignment amplitude, but their top-5 NON-consec lists differ
  => same peak, different functionals. Constructive-interference is an
  ANALOGY for the peak, not the measS7 mechanism (which is mod-7 arithmetic).

